      "text": "To find the measure of the smallest interior angle of a triangle where the angles are in the ratio of 5:6:7, we first need to determine the total number of parts that make up the sum of the interior angles of the triangle. The sum of the interior angles of any triangle is always 180 degrees.\n\nLet's denote the measures of the interior angles as \\(5x\\), \\(6x\\), and \\(7x\\) because they are in the ratio of 5:6:7. The sum of these angles is given by:\n\\[\n5x + 6x + 7x = 180\n\\]\n\nCombine the terms on the left side:\n\\[\n18x = 180\n\\]\n\nNext, solve for \\(x\\) by dividing both sides of the equation by 18:\n\\[\nx = \\frac{180}{18} = 10\n\\]\n\nNow, we can find the measures of the angles by substituting \\(x = 10\\) back into the expressions for each angle:\n\\[\n5x = 5 \\times 10 = 50\n\\]\n\\[\n6x = 6 \\times 10 = 60\n\\]\n\\[\n7x = 7 \\times 10 = 70\n\\]\n\nThe smallest interior angle is the one with the smallest measure, which is 50 degrees. Therefore, the measure of the smallest interior angle is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{50}\n\\]",
